## Why This Is Asked

Explores end-to-end ML system design addressing latency constraints, data privacy regulations, model drift, and deployment reliability in regulated fintech environments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time stream processing with sub-20ms latency requirements
- Multi-tenant data isolation under GDPR compliance
- Feature stores for online/offline feature consistency
- Hybrid ML + rule-based scoring for fraud detection
- Continuous monitoring with drift detection and calibration
- Canary deployment strategies with automated rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Hybrid scoring function combining ML predictions with rule-based evaluation
function calculateFraudScore(transaction, mlPrediction, businessRules) {
  const baseScore = mlPrediction.probability;
  const ruleScore = businessRules.evaluate(transaction);

  // Weighted combination for final fraud score
  const finalScore = (baseScore * 0.7) + (ruleScore * 0.3);

  return {
    score: finalScore,
    recommendation: finalScore > 0.8 ? 'block' : 'allow',
    confidence: mlPrediction.confidence,
    appliedRules: ruleScore.triggeredRules
  };
}
```

